The ones that can undergo metathesis reaction are: NaOH solution, K2CO3 solution and Ba(NO3)2 solution.
1) H2SO4 + 2NaOH = Na2SO4 + 2H2O, neutralization reaction to generate water;
2) H2SO4 + K2CO3 = K2SO4 + CO2↑ + H2O, generating CO2 gas;
3) H2SO4 + Ba(NO3)2 = BaSO4↓ + 2HNO3, forming a BaSO4 precipitate that is insoluble in water;
No obvious metathesis reaction occurs with NaCl solution, because the products Na2SO4 and HCl are easily soluble in water, and no gas, water or precipitation is additionally generated, which does not meet the conditions for the metathesis reaction to occur.

