The reaction occurs in a closed container: N2 + 3H2 ⇌ 2NH3, the concentration of N2 is 0.8 mol/L at the beginning of the reaction, and the concentration of N2 becomes 0.7 mol/L after 5 minutes. Request:
(1) The average reaction rate in this time period expressed in N2 (unit: mol·L^{-1}·min^{-1});
(2) The changes in H2 and NH3 concentrations during this time period;
(3) The average reaction rate in NH3 over the time period and verify the relationship between v(N2):v(H2):v(NH3) and the metric number of the chemical equation.

exercises.answer:
(1) v(N2) = -Δc(N2)/Δt = 0.1 mol·L^{-1} / 5 min = 0.020 mol·L^{-1}·min^{-1};
(2) From the equation N2 + 3H2 ⇌ 2NH3, Δc(N2):Δc(H2):Δc(NH3) = -1:-3:+2, we can get Δc(H2) = -0.3 mol·L^{-1}, Δc(NH3) = +0.2 mol·L^{-1};
(3) v(NH3) = Δc(NH3)/Δt = 0.2 mol·L^{-1} / 5 min = 0.040 mol·L^{-1}·min^{-1};
Verification: v(N2):v(H2):v(NH3) = 0.020:0.060:0.040 = 1:3:2, which is proportional to its measurement number 1:3:2, so \frac{v(N2)}{1} = \frac{v(H2)}{3} = \frac{v(NH3)}{2}.

